\title{xtx: Exact and Fast Model Matrices}
\description{
Builds model matrices that are identical, bit for bit, to those of
\code{\link[stats:model.matrix]{stats::model.matrix()}}, faster, and offers algebra on the design
without forming the dense matrix.
}
\section{Options}{

\code{options(xtx.threads = )} sets the number of threads of the dense fill
and of the kernels: an integer, \code{0} for all available threads, or a
number strictly between 0 and 1 for that fraction of them (rounded up).
Without the option, half of the available threads are used (rounded up,
as in fixest), and one thread during \verb{R CMD check}. The available threads
are those OpenMP reports, capped by the environment variable
\code{OMP_THREAD_LIMIT}; without OpenMP, one. A larger number is capped, and
an invalid value is an error at the next operation.

The dense fill and the row-wise kernels (\code{\%*\%}, \code{\link[=quadratic_diagonal]{quadratic_diagonal()}})
compute each row independently, so their results do not depend on the
number of threads. Sums over rows (\code{crossprod()}, \code{colSums()} and
\code{colMeans()}, with or without groups) split the rows into fixed blocks,
one per thread, whose sums are added in a fixed order: results are
identical for a given number of threads, and can differ in the last
digits between numbers of threads. Small problems run on one thread.
}

